    $( Abel's theorem.  If the power series ` sum_ n e. NN0 A ( n ) ( x ^ n ) `
       is convergent at ` 1 ` , then it is equal to the limit from "below",
       along a Stolz angle ` S ` (note that the ` M = 1 ` case of a Stolz angle
       is the real line ` [ 0 , 1 ] ` ).  (Continuity on ` S \ { 1 } ` follows
       more generally from ~ psercn .)  (Contributed by Mario Carneiro,
