    $( If P is on the segment AB and AQ = BQ, then PA ` x. ` PB =
       BQ<HTML><sup>2</sup></HTML> ` - ` PQ<HTML><sup>2</sup></HTML>.  This
       follows from two uses of ~ chordthmlem3 to show that
       PQ<HTML><sup>2</sup></HTML> = QM<HTML><sup>2</sup></HTML> ` + `
       PM<HTML><sup>2</sup></HTML> and BQ<HTML><sup>2</sup></HTML> =
       QM<HTML><sup>2</sup></HTML> ` + ` BM<HTML><sup>2</sup></HTML>, so
       BQ<HTML><sup>2</sup></HTML> ` - ` PQ<HTML><sup>2</sup></HTML> =
       (QM<HTML><sup>2</sup></HTML> ` + ` BM<HTML><sup>2</sup></HTML>) ` - `
       (QM<HTML><sup>2</sup></HTML> ` + ` PM<HTML><sup>2</sup></HTML>) =
       BM<HTML><sup>2</sup></HTML> ` - ` PM<HTML><sup>2</sup></HTML>,
       which equals PA ` x. ` PB by ~ chordthmlem4 .  (Contributed by David
       Moews, 28-Feb-2017.) $)
    chordthmlem5 $p |- ( ph -> ( ( abs ` ( P - A ) ) x. ( abs ` ( P - B ) ) ) =
                                ( ( ( abs ` ( B - Q ) ) ^ 2 ) -
                                  ( ( abs ` ( P - Q ) ) ^ 2 ) ) ) $=
