    $( Heron's formula gives the area of a triangle given only the side
       lengths.  If points A, B, C form a triangle, then the area of the
       triangle, represented here as ` ( 1 / 2 ) x. X x. Y x. abs ( sin O ) ` ,
       is equal to the square root of
       ` S x. ( S - X ) x. ( S - Y ) x. ( S - Z ) ` , where
