    $( Lemma for ~ log2ub .  The proof of ~ log2ub , which is simply the
       evaluation of ~ log2tlbnd for ` N = 4 ` , takes the form of the addition
       of five fractions and showing this is less than another fraction.  We
       could just perform exact arithmetic on these fractions, get a large
       rational number, and just multiply everything to verify the claim, but
       as anyone who uses decimal numbers for this task knows, it is often
       better to pick a common denominator ` d ` (usually a large power of
       ` 1 0 ` ) and work with the closest approximations of the form ` n / d `
       for some integer ` n ` instead.  It turns out that for our purposes it
       is sufficient to take ` d = ( 3 ^ 7 ) x. 5 x. 7 ` , which is also nice
       because it shares many factors in common with the fractions in question.
       (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 17-Apr-2015.) $)
