  czeta $a class zeta $.

  ${
    $d f k n s $.
    $( Define the Riemann zeta function.  This definition uses a series
       expansion of the alternating zeta function ~~? zetaalt that is
       convergent everywhere except ` 1 ` , but going from the alternating zeta
       function to the regular zeta function requires dividing by
       ` 1 - 2 ^ ( 1 - s ) ` , which has zeroes other than ` 1 ` .  To extract
       the correct value of the zeta function at these points, we extend the
       divided alternating zeta function by continuity.  (Contributed by Mario
       Carneiro, 18-Jul-2014.) $)
